{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And the men came upon the women.</b> Together with the women who volunteered, their husbands came to consent to the gift, so that the collectors would accept from them — for they accept from women only a small matter (Bava Kamma 119a)." "<b>And every man who waved a wave-offering of gold.</b> And along with the women who volunteered gold ornaments, there also came every man who waved a wave-offering of gold, as in the saying: 'a row that finished silver, silver; that finished gold, gold' — they were not mixed."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:28:16.855417792Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}